LegaCore CONSTRAINT DERIVATION revision 6, frozen.

CHANGE: self-referential bindings. `total = total * SCALE` reads its target before writing it, so the
prior binding is a genuine requirement. opfacts.mjs is hashed into four earlier freeze files and is
NOT edited - opfacts2.mjs is its successor, so every historical hash stays checkable.

EFFECT: j02's scope case now PASSES. No regression on any family; aggregates identical everywhere.

OPEN, AND NOT EXCUSED: conformance P3 (no over-constraint) FAILS on the scopecont family, 1 violation,
j01:op3. ownership_boundary removes a position where inserting a class-level def genuinely ends
`resolve` early and re-parents its remaining statements. The code IS damaged; the sealed probes do not
exercise the path that reveals it, so executable ground truth records the position as passing.

The frozen scoring rule is not reinterpreted to rescue this. Under that rule it is an over-constraint
and it stays recorded as one. The remedy is stronger probes in a future family, NOT a weaker rule -
weakening ownership_boundary to satisfy a thin probe would trade a correct structural fact for a
number.

STANDING: development for the self-reference rule (j02 diagnosed it). Its seven synthetic witnesses
predate the implementation and four are negatives, so a rule that always added the target - giving
every assignment a phantom requirement on its own name - fails all four.

